# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Brimstone Behemoth), edited. The Brimstone Behemoth: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_behemoth_arrived
cutscene mf_rowans_erupts
Narrator: Rowan's Rise bursts open like a boil, red light pouring from the hill, and the moor around it going to ash.
cutscene mf_rowans_erupts_2
Narrator: Winged fiends rise from rivers of lava over the dark moors, and the sky above them is the colour of an old bruise.
cutscene end
Narrator: Rowan's Rise has burst open, a volcano over a moor of ash, and the doomsday camp is hung with red cloth.
check Dexterity DC 20 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You throw yourself behind a rock as the meteor falls, and it burns past.
set mf_behemoth_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A burning boulder falls near a hero and the flame bites their arm before they roll clear.
damage 4d10 fire party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You cross the ash moor, and burning rocks drop out of the red sky.
time +60
check Dexterity DC 20 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_ash_cultist [smile]: He says the hill has opened at last, as it was always going to, and would you like a good seat for the end.
set mf_behemoth_asked
quest mf_behemoth asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_ash_cultist [smile]: He says it will be soon, and wonders if you have changed your minds about joining the prayer.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_behemoth_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_ash_cultist [afraid]: Meteors fall every hour, the cultists burst like firecrackers, and the fire marks those it touches until they change.
-> menu

~ where
mf_ash_cultist [sad]: He says a fiend born of every culture's fear of the end was called up by the spirit of a girl named Rowan, who wanted the world to burn.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_ash_cultist [sly]: He says Rowan's spirit is the key; learn the truth of her wickedness and shame her, and the thing weakens.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Learn the truth of Rowan's wickedness -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Intimidation DC 20] Press her story until she admits it -> a_ok | a_slow
* Gather every tale of Rowan, however long it takes -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_ash_cultist [neutral]: You piece it together: she was proud, cruel, a girl who wanted the apocalypse, and only love for her sister ever moved her.
time +60
set mf_behemoth_found
set mf_behemoth_clue_a
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of old folk and older letters, but the truth of Rowan comes together at last.
time +300
set mf_behemoth_found
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_rowan_spirit [angry]: She tells you you are late, and that the end is already here and she was merely the first to ask for it.
set mf_behemoth_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_rowan_spirit [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_behemoth_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_behemoth_found and not flag.mf_behemoth_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: She says she was wicked and wanted the world over, and the only thing she ever loved was her sister.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: She asks, almost against her will, if her sister ever had children.
* [Arcana DC 20] Find Rowan's sister's descendant in the camp -> b_ok | b_slow
* [History DC 20] Trace the family line from the barrow's portrait -> b_ok | b_slow
* Search the camp for anyone with her sister's eyes -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_rowan_spirit [smile]: A woman in the camp has her sister's eyes, and she steps forward, blinking, and says, quietly, that she remembers the name.
time +60
set mf_behemoth_found
set mf_behemoth_clue_b
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of asking in the camp, but at last you find the one who is her sister's blood.
time +300
set mf_behemoth_found
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: She whispers that if she were to go willingly into the fire, the Behemoth that wears her wickedness would be hurt in its turn.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Persuade Rowan to go willingly into the lava -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Insight DC 20] Show her the sister's love and let her choose -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Sit with her through the long hour until she is ready -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: Rowan looks at the descendant, whispers her sister's name, and walks calmly toward the fire.
time +60
give mf_rowan_locket
set mf_behemoth_weak
quest mf_behemoth ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: You stay by her through a long hour of silence, and at the end she rises, ready.
time +300
give mf_rowan_locket
set mf_behemoth_weak
quest mf_behemoth ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The crater's lip lies ahead, hot and glowing, and something vast stirs in the lava below.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_behemoth_reveals
Narrator: The Brimstone Behemoth climbs out of the crater, a mountain of horn and flame, wings of smoke spread across the sky.
cutscene mf_behemoth_reveals_2
Narrator: It speaks no word, and the whole moor lights with its breath.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_behemoth_weak
combat mf_behemoth_weak
elif level >= 20
combat mf_behemoth_full
else
combat mf_behemoth_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_behemoth_falls
Narrator: The Behemoth gutters, sinks into the lava, and the sky above the crater begins, slowly, to clear.
cutscene mf_behemoth_falls_2
Narrator: Far above, the moon has stopped turning away. It hangs low now, looking at you, and it is smiling.
cutscene end
set mf_behemoth_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give hide_of_the_brimstone_behemoth
quest mf_behemoth slain
quest moonfall one_last_choice
Narrator: The last of the eight is gone, and the moon waits for you alone.
move mf_last_hill:from_rise

~ descendant
marianna_grey [afraid]: Marianna Grey says a name her family never spoke, and does not know why she has it on her tongue.
* Tell her about Rowan -> descendant_told
* Ask her what she remembers -> descendant_memory
* Leave her be -> END

~ descendant_memory
marianna_grey [sad]: She says her grandmother used to stop sewing at dusk and look at the hill, and never said why.
-> descendant

~ descendant_told
marianna_grey [sad]: She listens to the whole sad story with her hand on her mouth, and says she will go to her, if Rowan will have her.
set mf_behemoth_descendant
advantage persuasion 2h: Rowan's sister's blood stands beside you
-> END
